            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            is a simplicial incarnation of the notion of a
            %em boundary segment
            (as opposed to the full boundary) of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell"} cell
          %p
            Specifically, the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda_k[n] \hookrightarrow \Delta[n]
            of the
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            (defined for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ZeroSimplexHasNoHorns"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+simplex"} boundary of the n-simplex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta^n
            of the standard simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-simplex"} n-simplex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
            by discarding its
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            The property of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            to have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            against the inclusions of horns into their simplices (have “horn fillers”) characterizes the basic types of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
                (hence
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                against
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em all horns
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left%2Fright+Kan+fibrations"} left/right Kan fibrations
                are characterized as having the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                against all horns
                %em except
                possibly the first/last horn inclusion in each dimension, respectively;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
                are characterized as having the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                against all horns
                %em except
                possibly the first and last horn inclusion in each dimension, respectively.
          %p
            Specifically,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            are the simplicial analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibrations"} Serre fibrations
            (in a precise sense so under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} on topological spaces
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disk"} disk
            into its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi id
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Lambda_k[n] \hookrightarrow \Delta[n]
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  \\overset{\left\vert-\right\vert}{\mapsto}
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  D^{n-1} \overset{(id,0)}{\hookrightarrow} D^{n-1} \times [0,1]
                  \\,,
          %p
            as both are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+cofibrations"} generating cofibrations
            in their respective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"}> on sSet
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} on Top
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Simp
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta[n] = \mathbf{\Delta}( -, [n]) \in  Simp Set
          %p
            denote the standard simplicial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimpSet"} SimpSet
          #Horn.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (horns)
            %p
              For all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n, k \,\in\, \mathbb{N}
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\leq k \leq n
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,k)
                \-horn
              or
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,k)
                \-box
              is the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} sub
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Lambda_k[n]
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    \\Delta[n]
            %p
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of all faces
              %em except
              the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p#InnerHorns
              This is called an
              %strong outer horn
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n
              = succeed "." do
                %strong inner horn
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
              make sense and they are calculated objectwise, thus in this case dimensionwise. This way it becomes clear what the structure of a horn as a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^k[n]: \Delta^{op} \to Set
              must therefore be: it takes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m]
              to the collection of ordinal maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon [m] \to [n]
              which factor through some coface map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n-1] \to [n]
              which is
              %em not
              the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
          #ZeroSimplexHasNoHorns.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (the 0-simplex has no horns)
              %br/
              Beware that any would-be horn of the 0-simplex (whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+simplex"} boundary
              is the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+simplicial+set"} empty simplicial set
              = succeed "-cluded" do
                %em ex
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Horn"}
              %em no
              horn.
            %p
              This is not a matter of convention if one sticks to the usual definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              as having
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting
              against
              = succeed ":" do
                %em all horns
              %em not
              declare a would-be horn of the 0-simplex to be itself the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+simplicial+set"} empty simplicial set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+of+a+category"} nerve
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+groupoid"} empty groupoid
              fail to be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KanComplex"}
            %p
              Conversely, the fact that every horn is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              means (see also
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Kan+fibration#KanFibrationNeedNotBeSurjective"} this Example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+simplicial+set"} empty simplicial set
              (an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+bundle"} empty bundle
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∅
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varnothing \to X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KanFibration"}
            %p
              This is in contrast to the situation for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+Kan+fibrations"} acyclic Kan fibrations
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "acyclic+Kan+fibration#AcyclicKanFibrationsAreSurjective"} there
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a{:href => "#InnerHorns"} inner horn
              of the 2-simplex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
